  "prediction": "This report provides an overview of cybersecurity-related bills and hearings in the U.S. Congress during the 115th and 116th sessions. In the 116th Congress, the House has passed four cybersecurity bills, and the Senate has considered four others, passing one. A total of 31 bills received committee consideration or passed one or both chambers in the 115th Congress, and five of these bills were signed into law. These laws include the Department of Energy Research and Innovation Act, the John S. McCain National Defense Authorization Act, and the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017. The report also lists cybersecurity-related hearings in the 116th Congress, arranged by date and committee. However, the list should not be considered definitive as no single, objective selection criterion was used to identify which hearings to include. For more information on cybersecurity legislation and related issues, the report provides links to various Congressional Research Service reports.",
  "scored_prediction": "This report provides an overview of cybersecurity-related bills and hearings in the U.S. Congress during the 115th and 116th sessions. In the 116th Congress, the House has passed four cybersecurity bills, and the Senate has considered four others, passing one. A total of 31 bills received committee consideration or passed one or both chambers in the 115th Congress, and five of these bills were signed into law. These laws include the Department of Energy Research and Innovation Act, the John S. McCain National Defense Authorization Act, and the National Defense Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2017. The report also lists cybersecurity-related hearings in the 116th Congress, arranged by date and committee. However, the list should not be considered definitive as no single, objective selection criterion was used to identify which hearings to include. For more information on cybersecurity legislation and related issues, the report provides links to various Congressional Research Service reports.",
  "score": 31.213872344548776,
  "answers": [
    "Most major cybersecurity legislative provisions were enacted prior to 2002, despite many recommendations having been made over the past decade. More recently, in the 115th and 116th Congresses, cybersecurity legislation has received either committee or floor action or final passage, and both chambers have held multiple hearings. In the 116th Congress, a number of House and Senate bills have received consideration, and hearings have been held by committees in each chamber. In the 115th Congress, 31 bills received some type of action (committee consideration or passage by one or both chambers). Five bills became public law. The House held 54 hearings on cybersecurity issues and the Senate held 40 hearings."
  ],
